1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:04,771
Survey teams around the world reset their tablets between rounds.

2
00:00:04,771 --> 00:00:14,906
That reset is the moment an unsent record or photo is lost for good, and the server's received count can't tell you what is still only on the device.

3
00:00:14,906 --> 00:00:17,558
LastCopy gives every tablet one answer:

4
00:00:17,558 --> 00:00:20,075
safe to wipe, recover first, or hold.

5
00:00:20,775 --> 00:00:23,167
A record can arrive without its photo.

6
00:00:23,167 --> 00:00:27,637
A spreadsheet can look short when the server actually has every answer.

7
00:00:27,637 --> 00:00:31,100
And a form can sit unsent while the totals still match.

8
00:00:31,800 --> 00:00:33,781
Agents decide where to look.

9
00:00:33,781 --> 00:00:35,550
Code decides what's true.

10
00:00:35,550 --> 00:00:38,380
A Meterless World Model plans each step.

11
00:00:38,380 --> 00:00:41,493
A Scout queries Zetaris across every source.

12
00:00:41,493 --> 00:00:49,275
Nemotron forms and critiques hypotheses, and a deterministic verifier settles them against the original bytes.

13
00:00:49,975 --> 00:00:52,538
This is a real connected run from today.

14
00:00:52,538 --> 00:00:58,689
Zetaris answers every query, and every judgement call is Nemotron, through Meterless Nightshift.

15
00:00:58,689 --> 00:01:00,547
Watch the World Model's plan.

16
00:01:00,547 --> 00:01:06,633
The Reviewer sends all five hypotheses back, so the graph loops before any evidence is fetched.

17
00:01:06,633 --> 00:01:14,450
Then the verifier compares the original bytes and confirms or refutes each hypothesis, and only then does the gate decide.

18
00:01:15,150 --> 00:01:26,237
Each tablet gets a decision made by code, a hashed certificate, and a plain sentence written by Nemotron, where every ID and filename is checked against the evidence.

19
00:01:26,237 --> 00:01:31,150
Tablet two must recover first, because one photo never reached the server.

20
00:01:31,850 --> 00:01:34,555
The rule itself is simple enough to try.

21
00:01:34,555 --> 00:01:41,114
Missing data always beats looks fine, and a tablet that never exported is never treated as clean.

22
00:01:41,114 --> 00:01:43,075
No model can reach this rule.

23
00:01:43,775 --> 00:01:54,075
Judges can run the whole loop in four seconds, with no keys, and re-verify any certificate against the original archives, independently of LastCopy.

24
00:01:54,775 --> 00:01:55,494
LastCopy.

25
00:01:55,494 --> 00:01:59,250
Wipe a tablet only after its last copy is safe.
